{
  "name": "tamper-evident-logs",
  "description": "Design and build a tamper-evident audit log end to end: model the threat and requirements, pick SHA-256 and an RFC 8785 canonical form, design the append-only record and hash chain, implement canonical hashing and crash-safe append writers per stack, generate and store Ed25519 keys with rotation, build a Merkle tree with inclusion and consistency proofs, sign and externally anchor checkpoints, rotate logs without breaking the chain, and ship stack-specific verifiers proven by a tamper detection test suite.",
